{"kind":"artifact","text":"Candidate at docs for the fan-out contract-full verdict, exact head fd513938b257a83cc998d9fea7cefdf3543198b3.\n\nWHAT CHANGED HERE. docs/reference/performance.md only. It states the verdict for the versioned consecutive fan-out axis clause by clause against adopted proposal e5b88d52 and the conditions of request e1ab6474, reports every width in both relative and millisecond terms, and re-anchors onto the live artifacts for the behaviour it describes: cmd/gitseq-perf f0047ba0, internal/perflane 86288a0f and performance 4da5ebd0, all at merge de9a2b83. The predecessors it previously named were retired by that merge.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT. Every number comes from one full-tier run I made and verified myself, measured at f71b4d73, an ancestor of this head, with contract digest b0795bc7 which I recomputed from performance/contract-v2.json rather than reading back, and one fixture exact digest d15f714d across all samples. 505 records: 100 primary samples at each of widths 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256 plus one round-zero diagnostic per width. I checked all 500 primary trusted-versus-projected digest pairs and found zero mismatches. The raw samples are tracked at this same head under performance/retained/fanout-20260819-f71b4d73, so every figure on the page is recomputable rather than taken on trust. Nothing derived is stored beside them.\n\nCOSTS PER WIDTH against the width-one p50 of 471.761 ms: -7.292 ms and -1.546 percent at width 8, -32.199 ms and -6.825 percent at 16, -28.573 ms and -6.057 percent at 64, and -29.246 ms and -6.199 percent at 256. No clamping, no magnitudes, no cross-case pairing. The only increase between adjacent widths is +3.626 ms from 16 to 64; the largest absolute step is the fall of -24.907 ms from 8 to 16.\n\nTHE VERDICT AND HOW IT SURVIVES ITS OWN DENOMINATOR. A sibling lane started two test processes a minute into measurement and load peaked at 14.53. Width one runs first and is the axis's sole denominator, so the disturbance landed there: 36 of its samples exceed 600 ms, all in rounds 46 to 93, and no other width has a single one, the largest outside width one being 598.181 ms. Rather than choose a denominator and hope, the page classifies against four — full-block p50 471.761, full-block simple median 474.324, pre-disturbance rounds 1 to 25 median 448.474, and contaminated rounds 76 to 100 median 735.251. PREVIEW and FIRST-PRODUCTION pass on all four. The worst case anywhere is width 8 at +3.566 percent against a +10 percent limit. The page says plainly that the classification is robust while the magnitudes are not, and refuses to quote the -6 and -36.8 percent figures as fan-out speedups.\n\nIt also discloses that width 8 carries the tail of the disturbance, quarters 496.527, 490.666, 456.593, 440.960. Since width 8 is the worst-case width against every denominator, the run's worst figure is inflated by residual load and the true cost there is lower than any number published. The page discloses the restart history too: an earlier invocation was suspended by machine sleep and discarded whole rather than repaired, because sample records carry no wall-clock timestamp and a spanning suspend cannot be found afterwards in the data.\n\nMISSES, REPORTED NOT HIDDEN. The fixed one-base append is about nine times its separate 50 ms budget, which belongs to parked request 8add6909 and is named as such. The page refuses two implications the evidence cannot support: that a passing ratio says anything about append latency overall, and that a depth-1,000 result is a cross-product result at depth 50,000 or 500,000. The 10 percent allowance is worth between 44.847 and 73.525 ms at this run's denominators, at or above the whole absolute budget, which is why the two targets stay apart.\n\nThe previous campaign's numbers, digests and head appear nowhere. Its raw files no longer exist, and it reported the same pass, so the contract's inconclusiveness rule is not triggered by replacing it.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 26 packages, zero failures, docset uncached at 63.293 seconds. gofmt clean, working tree clean. Pushed; merge-base with origin/main is 92dd2df1 itself.\n\nPredecessor at this path is fa35d881, live and not stale when I checked immediately before publishing. Retirement belongs to the merge, not here. I have not merged.","body":{"commit":"fd513938b257a83cc998d9fea7cefdf3543198b3","path":"docs"}}